deck "Event Ingest, End to End" (
  author: "Dana Reyes"
  venue: "Platform guild review"
  aspect: 16:9
  canvas: 1600x900
  theme: "paper"
  language: en
)

slide architecture "How an event becomes queryable" (
  background: "paper"
  transition: none
) """
% Figure styles. Style expansion is authored source: the canvas may honour it
% but must not claim to own, name, or rewrite it.
\tikzset{
  stage/.style={
    draw=blue!55!black,
    fill=blue!8,
    rounded corners=2pt,
    very thick,
    text width=26mm,
    align=center,
    minimum height=11mm,
    font=\small
  },
  store/.style={
    draw=teal!60!black,
    fill=teal!8,
    rounded corners=6pt,
    thick,
    text width=24mm,
    align=center,
    minimum height=13mm,
    font=\small
  },
  gate/.style={
    draw=orange!70!black,
    fill=orange!14,
    circle,
    thick,
    minimum size=14mm,
    font=\footnotesize\bfseries
  },
  card/.style={
    draw=black!45,
    fill=white,
    rounded corners=3pt,
    line width=0.8pt,
    text width=52mm,
    font=\small
  },
  flow/.style={-stealth, very thick, draw=blue!55!black},
  trace/.style={-{Latex[length=2.4mm]}, thick, dashed, draw=black!55}
}

\node[anchor=north west, text width=90mm, style=display] (title) at (1,8.4) {
How an event becomes queryable
};

% Ingest path. The first stage is placed absolutely; the next two follow it.
\node[stage, anchor=north west] (edge-collector) at (1,6.4) {
**Edge collector**\\
HTTP and gRPC
};

\node[stage, right=12mm of edge-collector] (decode) {
**Decode**\\
schema registry
};

\node[stage, right=12mm of decode] (enrich) {
**Enrich**\\
tenant and geo
};

\node[gate, below=14mm of enrich] (overflow) {\(p_{99}\)};

\node[store, anchor=north west] (hot-store) at (11.9,6.4) {
**Hot store**\\
7 days, columnar
};

\node[store, anchor=north west] (query-api) at (11.9,3.9) {
**Query API**\\
SQL and PromQL
};

\node[
  draw=black!55,
  fill=black!4,
  rounded corners=2pt,
  thick,
  text width=22mm,
  align=center,
  font=\footnotesize,
  anchor=north
] (audit-log) at (5.2,1.4) {
Append-only audit log
};

\node[card, anchor=north west] (contract) at (1,3.9) {
What the team actually promises:

1. **At-least-once** delivery into the hot store.
2. Decode failures land in the dead-letter topic — never silently dropped.
3. Enrichment happens before routing, so a tenant is never guessed.

<div class="sla">
  Edge-to-queryable budget: \(p_{99} \le 250\,\mathrm{ms}\).
</div>
};

\node[anchor=north west, text width=48mm, style=body] (budget) at (6.9,3.4) {
The stage budget people argue about:
\[
  \sum_{s \in \mathrm{stages}} t_s + t_{\mathrm{commit}} \le 250\,\mathrm{ms}.
\]
<span class="hint">Measured at the edge, not at the broker.</span>
};

% Straight flow along the ingest path.
\draw[flow] (edge-collector) -- (decode);
\draw[flow] (decode) -- (enrich);
\draw[flow] (enrich.east) -- (hot-store.west);
\draw[flow] (enrich.south) -- node[right, font=\footnotesize] {over budget} (overflow.north);

% Orthogonal flow. Storage feeds the query surface; decode and the overflow
% gate both report to the audit log.
\draw[flow] (hot-store.south) |- (query-api.west);
\draw[trace] (decode.south) -| (audit-log.north);
\draw[trace] (overflow.south) -| (audit-log.east);

% Deliberately expanded region: the shard fan-out is generated, so no authored
% node identity or coordinate exists to write back to.
\foreach \region [count=\index] in {eu, us, ap} {
  \node[store, text width=16mm, minimum height=7mm, font=\footnotesize]
    (shard-\region) at ($(hot-store.south east) + (0.9, -0.8*\index)$) {Shard \region};
}

% Deliberately transformed region: a decorative shadow behind the ingest path,
% expressed with a scope transformation and a computed rectangle.
\begin{scope}[shift={(0.12,-0.12)}, opacity=0.18]
  \path[fill=black!45, rounded corners=2pt]
    (edge-collector.north west) rectangle (enrich.south east);
\end{scope}

% Deliberately computed placement: this tag hangs off another node's border.
\node[anchor=west, font=\footnotesize\itshape, text=black!60] (sla-tag)
  at ([xshift=4mm]query-api.east) {gate at p99};
"""

note """
Walk the top row left to right, then drop to the audit log.

Two honest caveats when this slide is on screen:

- the shard row is generated, so it is illustrative rather than exact;
- the budget only holds while the enrich cache is warm.

Ask whether anyone has measured the edge-to-queryable path end to end.
"""

slide backpressure "Where backpressure actually bites" (
  background: "paper"
  transition: fade
) """
\node[anchor=north west, text width=90mm, style=display] (heading) at (1,8.4) {
Where backpressure actually bites
};

\node[
  draw=orange!70!black,
  fill=orange!12,
  circle,
  thick,
  minimum size=18mm,
  font=\footnotesize\bfseries,
  anchor=center
] (queue) at (4,5.6) {queue};

\node[
  draw=blue!55!black,
  fill=blue!8,
  rounded corners=2pt,
  very thick,
  text width=30mm,
  align=center,
  anchor=center
] (consumer) at (8.6,5.6) {
**Consumer group**\\
8 workers
};

\node[
  draw=red!60!black,
  fill=red!8,
  rounded corners=2pt,
  thick,
  text width=30mm,
  align=center,
  anchor=center
] (dead-letter) at (13.2,2.8) {
**Dead letter**\\
replayable
};

\node[anchor=north west, text width=62mm, style=body] (reading) at (1,3.4) {
Read the queue depth, not the CPU graph:

- depth flat, latency rising: the consumer is slow;
- depth rising, latency flat: the producer is bursting;
- both rising: you are already late.

<div class="rule">
  Lag is a queue property, so
  \(\mathrm{lag} = \mathrm{offset}_{\mathrm{head}} - \mathrm{offset}_{\mathrm{commit}}\).
</div>
};

\draw[-stealth, very thick, draw=blue!55!black] (queue) -- (consumer);
\draw[-{Latex[length=2.4mm]}, thick, dashed, draw=red!60!black]
  (consumer.south) |- (dead-letter.west);

% Deliberately expanded region: worker lanes are drawn by a loop over computed
% offsets, so they are decoration rather than authored objects.
\foreach \lane in {1,2,3,4} {
  \draw[draw=black!25, line width=0.4pt]
    ([yshift=\lane*1.4mm]consumer.west) -- ([yshift=\lane*1.4mm]consumer.east);
}

% Deliberately computed placement.
\node[anchor=south, font=\footnotesize\itshape, text=black!60] (depth-tag)
  at ([yshift=7mm]queue.north) {depth = lag};
"""

note """
The three-case reading is the whole point of this slide.

Do not promise a fix here; the next slide in the real talk is the capacity
review, and that is a budget conversation rather than an engineering one.
"""
